thout declared\neffects/grants. Reject ambient config reads and secret leakage in logs,\nmanifests, source maps, prompts, traces or diagnostics; only policy-allowed\nredacted markers may appear. Capture build-time reads as reproducibility inputs\nor reject them in hermetic builds. Closing evidence is the versioned reload\npolicy, typed manifest/source-precedence/secret records, accepted/rejected\nreload fixtures and redaction report. Emit applicable S8 diagnostics including\nS8-RELOAD with config/field/source/span-or-edge, effect/grant, secret/redaction\nstate and remediation. Dependencies consume S1/S2 schema/decoding and Runtime\nlifecycle, SAFE10/SAFE11/R11 grants/taint and R12 observations; loader generation\nalone does not prove an actual reload.\n\nCriterion `schema/semantic-compatibility-diff/decision-interface` (Open): Input: Exact old/new schema identities, expanded source and generated projection contracts, and additive/migration-required/binary-stable/reviewed-breaking/append-only/exact compatibility policy. Outputs: Semantic diff and compatibility report; Required migration/review decisions; Accepted and rejected evolution fixtures. Accept: Classify added/removed/renamed fields, changed nullability/enums/variants/refinements/binary layouts and semantic hazards. Include GraphQL resolver policy, HTTP route/error/auth, database dialect/migration, ABI and artifact-schema changes; preserve public schema-library consumer context when those adapters are used. Emit the required compatibility/migration decision for each changed boundary instead of accepting a textual-only diff. Refuse: Changed schema/projection without declared policy or required migration/review evidence; Hidden API/client/AI or ABI compatibility breaks and weakened constraints; Wrong from/to identity, dropped negative condition or schema helper availability substituted for a checked diff. Dependencies consume actual artifacts: S1 old/new schemas and S4/S5/S6/S7/S9 projection/consumer records; S