uted, :hosted or an explicitly legal bridged profile. Reject: Reject an AI construct in an unbridged profile outside :ai, :distributed or :hosted; a backend or runtime adapter cannot legalize it. Required output: Compile-time AI profile legality report naming the selected profile and explicit bridge, with accepted and rejected expanded-form fixtures. Preserve the source facets, conditional rules, diagnostic context and dependencies pinned in this per-ID proposal. Dependencies consume actual outputs, not whole-task completion.\n<!-- domains-task-projection/ai:end -->\n\n## GPU\n\nKey `gpu`; owner role: accelerator compiler maintainer. Purpose: preserve kernel\nmemory-space and synchronization semantics. Scope: kernel IR, workgroup shape,\nbarriers, vectorization and declared target features; not universal accelerator\nsupport. Input: checked kernels and target manifest. Output: GPU IR, kernel\nartifact and memory/synchronization diagnostics. Governed by\n[GPU contract](../phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/136-dom13-gpu-and-accelerator-computing-domain-specification.md).\n\n<!-- domains-task-projection/gpu:start -->\nOutcome: kernels execute on the adopted target with validated memory/barrier\nbehavior. Remaining tasks, all open: adopt target and kernel ABI; implement GPU\nIR/checking; lower kernel and host dispatch; execute numeric/result and illegal\nmemory-space/barrier fixtures. Yes/no acceptance: do kernels produce the\nspecified results? Are invalid synchronization and target features rejected?\nIntegration: MIR/Legality, Lower/Emit, explicit Runtime dispatch. Decision owner:\naccelerator maintainer; recommendation: one named reference target first,\nadditional targets only by their own conformance evidence. Target choice is\nnot silently adopted by this roadmap.\n\nP11 profile interface: emit host/device argument/address-space/layout/alignment/alias/lifetime, transfer/synchronization and feature/workgroup/launch/occupancy records. Reject host services in kernels, use-after-free/double release/unsynchronized host reads, unsupported launch/features and invalid barriers; safe sharing needs provider evidence. Preserve precision/rounding/fusion/denormal/approximation/provider/certificate facts through lowering or diagnose. ABI production, kernel/launch checks, buffer validity and actual Runtime transfers remain separate interfaces; a graph is not executed transfer evidence.\n\nCriterion profile-gap/gpu/host-device-boundary (Open): Input: Separate host orchestration and GPU kernel artifacts with argument address-space/layout/alignment/alias/lifetime and declared target feature/workgroup/grid/occupancy/launch configuration. Accept: Validate kernel-only legality, construct the typed host/device ABI boundary and transfer/lifetime records, and check target launch/features independently. Host profile remains explicit; device orchestration cannot import ambient host semantics into a kernel. Reject: Host IO/reflection/eval/allocation/GC/exceptions/ordinary threads in kernels, unsupported recursion/dispatch, missing argument or transfer boundary, invalid target or launch configuration. Required outputs: Host/device and target/launch/occupancy manifests, kernel IR, typed argument ABI and accepted/rejected kernel/launch/feature fixtures with kernel/buffer/address-space/origin context. Dependencies: backend-interface, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping gpu/host-device-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/gpu/memory-synchronization (Open): Input: