ime outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n<!-- domains-task-projection/ui:end -->\n\n## Rollup and nonclaims\n\nIntegration reads the named outcomes above, not a duplicate task list. None is\nclosed by this proposal. Shared semantic fact transport does not merge domain\nownership, and a future target decision does not block unrelated compiler work.\nExisting planning references remain traceability; new implementation namespaces\nshould use these semantic subsystem names without whimsical codename prefixes.\n\n\n## Additional integration task views\n\nThese nine Open task interfaces implement declared application slices within Domains. They add no completed component or product claim.\n\n### Typed automation and action audit\n\n<!-- domains-task-projection/automation:start -->\nOutcome: Typed automation and action audit with source-bound artifacts and rejection behavior. Remaining tasks, all open: execute every explicit criterion below on its named target/provider; retain actual artifacts and failure diagnostics.\n\nCriterion `domain/automation-plan-audit`: Produce declared dry-run/audit records of planned writes/deletes/deployments/commands without hiding the eventual effect contract. Accepted fixture: Produce a dry-run of writes/deletes/deployments/commands and compare it with the authorized actual action audit. Negative fixture: Reject omitted effects, misleading dry-run authority or unredacted secret-bearing audit fields. Required evidence: dry-run plan and source-linked action audit; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/en