ejected? Integration: MIR/Schema,\nRuntime durability, AI review steps, Stdlib workflows. Decision owner: workflow\nmaintainer; recommendation: versioned event log as replay input, explicit\nprovider boundary for storage rather than a hidden database choice.\n\nDOM9 acceptance also requires declared CRDT identity/order/merge/update and\nserialization laws, causal history, offline authorization, conflict visibility,\ntombstone/compaction and migration policy. Classify coordination as free,\nrequired or deferred; reject nonmonotonic rules without an explicit mechanism.\nThe checkout fixture must not double-charge on replay. The local-first cart\nfixture must converge after partition/heal, duplicate/reordered delivery,\nrestart and migration, and reject invalid merge laws or hidden intent loss.\nDependencies: Schema state/event versions, Runtime durable storage/replay and\nAuth grants. These criteria add no acceptance credit or provider selection. P9 profile interface: emit typed step input/output/effect/grant/retry/timeout/cancellation/idempotency/compensation and event/replay records; validate versioned messages and persisted state with migration/taint/retention/order/delivery policy. Execute recovery separately from admitted step construction; replay must consume recorded nondeterminism without repeating external actions. Reject schema drift without migration, untyped external failure, unrecorded replay inputs and missing required compensation. Service-boundary admission consumes Schema/Auth and Runtime facts, not their whole-task completion.\n\nCriterion profile-gap/distributed/durable-step-contract (Open): Input: Workflow graph and step input/output schemas, declared effects/grants, idempotency key, retry/timeout/cancellation/compensation and failure policy. Accept: Construct typed step records and durable transitions; execute admitted external steps with declared idempotency; execute failure/retry/timeout/cancel/compensation transitions separately; replay recorded results/decisions without repeating the recorded external action. Retain human-review state where applicable. Reject: Untyped external failure, missing required idempotency/compensation or timeout/failure contract, ambient grants, raw device operations and unrecorded nondeterminism in replay-sensitive steps. Required outputs: Workflow graph, typed step table, event-log/persistence boundary records, retry/timeout/compensation table, replay policy/schema and accepted/rejected recovery fixtures. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution, schema, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping distributed/durable-step-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/distributed/message-state-boundary (Open): Input: Message, persisted state and service endpoint with schema/version, compatibility/migration, taint/retention, delivery/order and relevant idempotency policies. Accept: Validate transport input/output against the named schemas, apply or reject state/schema migrations under replay compatibility, enforce data-sink taint/retention, and admit services only with declared effect/grant/timeout/retry/error and required backpressure/circuit-breaker policy. Reject: Schemaless boundary, version drift without migration, untyped service failure, ambient service authority and missing delivery/order or required side-effect policy. Required outputs: Message schema bundle, migration result, service capability/error boundary manifest, state persistence and delivery/ordering conformance records. Dependencies: schema, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution, au