   "# Standard Library\n\nWorking name: **Standard Library** (proposed). Semantic key: `stdlib`.\nOwner role: library maintainer; current owner unassigned by this proposal.\nBaseline: `c21068a6d39259b7110845bbbcefaf9bf6901232`.\n\nImplementation task authority: [Spec Kit ledger](../../specs/stdlib-workflow/tasks.md#implementation-tasks).\nEdit the ledger and run `clojure -M tools/stdlib_task_projection.clj --write`;\nthe remaining-task table below is generated.\n\n## Purpose and scope\n\nProvide real profile-aware APIs, not host-language escape hatches. The finite\nmodule inventory is the [standard-library contract index](../phase-16-standard-library/README.md).\nOwn exports, manifests, safe wrappers and examples; compiler language forms,\nruntime providers and platform implementation remain separate components.\n\n## Release outcome\n\nThe contract inventory's modules have implemented exports, profile/effect/\ncapability/allocation/stability metadata, executable API examples and rejected\nprofile/authority fixtures. Unsupported profile/module pairs are explicit.\nFull platform modules consume Platform outcomes rather than implying them.\nOutcome open; this does not promote metadata coverage to functioning libraries.\n\n## Interfaces and dependencies\n\nInputs: typed language operations, runtime/provider APIs and module schemas.\nOutputs: compiled modules, export manifests, documentation examples, unsafe\nisland audits and compatibility evidence. Core/Types/Effects/Legality/Auth are\nrequired for compiled API acceptance; Runtime is required only for serviced\nAPIs. Pure library algorithms and fixtures can develop earlier with the seed.\nBuild consumes manifests later, so no circular build prerequisite exists.\n\n## Remaining tasks and evidence\n\n<!-- stdlib-task-projection:start -->\n| Task (all open) | Evidence baseline | Closing evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Reconcile export inventory with actual callable implementations | [Library source artifact](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/foundation/00499-standard-library-source-artifact.clj) | Per-export source/implementation/fixture map, with absent exports explicitly open; compiled module manifests agree with package metadata, documentation and conformance discovery on namespace/artifact identity, callable exports, profiles, effects, capabilities, allocation, errors, safety and stability. Reject missing or inconsistent metadata, undeclared effects, missing grants, host-dependent core exports and unaudited unsafe internals with STD1001-STD1008 as applicable. Apply the source-specific acceptance and dependency matrix in plan.md. Source obligation `language/library/enforce-portability-layers`: Reject an upward dependency from a lower standard-library portability layer and report the exact namespaces shipped for the selected profile. Accept: Publish the L13 namespace-to-layer inventory for compiler core(0), portable data(1), memory/resources/concurrency(2), capability-backed host/platform(3) and domain/compiler libraries(4). Check actual dependency edges and emit the exact shipped namespace subset for each selected profile; higher-to-lower dependencies are permitted. Reject: Reject a lower-layer dependency on a higher layer, an undeclared namespace/layer or a profile manifest claiming an unavailable namespace; hosted-only convenience cannot silently define the lower layers. Required outputs: Source/actual layer and dependency graph, exact per-profile namespace availability manifest, allowed downward-edge and rejected upward-edge fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Decision criterion interface/language/library/publish-public-contract: Publish machine-readable namespace/operation contracts for profile/type/effect/capability, allocation/resource, error/panic, blocking/nondeterminism and stability semantics; bind them to actual exports. Reject: Reject missing/false export metadata, hidden host behavior, untracked authority and public declarations inconsistent with callable implementations. Required outputs: Versioned public API/export/profile manifests and contract-to-implementation conformance/denial evidence. |\n| Complete pure core, collections, text, numeric and testing APIs | [Library architecture](../phase-16-standard-library/211-std1-standard-library-architecture.md) | Compiled examples and type/arity/value rejection through real APIs; STD2-STD5 and STD14 fixtures preserve evaluation order, transfers, inert stored values, original persistent values, Unicode boundaries, explicit numeric modes and structured test evidence. Retain each operation's proven-presence/nonempty/in-range premise without invented fallback, coercion, static facts or provider guarantees. Reject invalid UTF-8, implicit locale/lossy conversion, unchecked partial operations, unproved math transformations, free-text-only diagnostic matching and ungranted live-service tests. Compile documentation under every claimed profile; require the exact outputs and negative cases in plan.md. Decision criterion interface/language/effects/interpret-test-fixture: Interpret declared test fixture handlers with typed request/result, explicit effect allowance and stable fixture setup/teardown semantics; retain original handler labels and captures. Reject: Reject handler request/response mismatch, hidden fixture authority, illegal continuation/capture lifetime or unsupported profile behavior. Required outputs: Typed fixture-handler contract, setup/body/teardown result and failure diagnostics, accepted and rejected fixture cases. Decision criterion interface/language/library/access-ordered-vector: Implement ordered indexed Vector values with declared persistence, index legality and stable e