mplicit cross-tenant sharing, retrieved instruction authority, incompatible index reuse and fresh retrieval where a recorded result is required. Record query/result ids, scores, embedding identity and old/new embedding lineage. Deletion/redaction must remove stale retrievable entries and update indexes and ledgers. The semantic producer retains its compilation, policy and provider responsibilities. This library leaf must expose the same accepted/refused predicate through its own callable boundary, retaining actual call/results, typed failures, schema/effect/grant/replay/origin identities as applicable. Reject a bypassed or weakened check, a mismatched provider result, or an export/manifest name used instead of actual API invocation. This is consumer acceptance, not new evidence that the underlying service or API is implemented. Library consumer criteria interface/behavior/a9/eval-gate, interface/behavior/a9/eval-subject-binding, interface/behavior/a9/metric-decision: Invoke the actual STD13 public API against declared Domain/Runtime providers under this retained semantic contract: A9: produce versioned dataset/schema/provenance/split artifacts and eval reports bound to every behavior-changing subject/model/prompt/tool/memory/policy/runtime identity. Record changed artifacts, metric direction/threshold/aggregation and confidence/sample or variance rules, seeds/traces, redacted samples or hashes, probe results and release decisions. Required safety probes cover injection, tool misuse, denial, schema failure, refusal and protected-data leakage. Reject absent/stale/incompatible release evidence, name-similarity fallback, missing probes or thresholds and unauthorized live-provider evaluation; preserve real credentials, provider spend/account policy and report-signing requirements. The semantic producer retains its compilation, policy and provider responsibilities. This library leaf must expose the same accepted/refused predicate through its own callable boundary, retaining actual call/results, typed failures, schema/effect/grant/replay/origin identities as applicable. Reject a bypassed or weakened check, a mismatched provider result, or an export/manifest name used instead of actual API invocation. This is consumer acceptance, not new evidence that the underlying service or API is implemented. |\n| Implement compiler and syntax adapters | [Module inventory](../phase-16-standard-library/README.md) | Own the STD15 public library boundary: Invoke the public meta API against actual syntax and compiler services under declared scoped authority. Required outputs: Callable compiler/syntax inspection/transform API preserving phases, hygiene, source, metadata and pass invalidation. Negative acceptance: Reject hidden compiler mutation, lost origins/hygiene, stale facts and ungranted phase access. Consume actual interface artifacts from syntax/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/syntax5-integrate-consumers, pipeline, plugins; naming a service does not implement it or require whole-component completion. Shared adapter source conditions below apply only to this API's subject, not its siblings. Implementation acceptance remains Open. STD15 requires actual syntax construction/inspection/transform APIs to preserve spans, hygiene, namespace, metadata and phase; C3 defines the underlying syntax representation and internal transform rules. Retain the library-call outcome separately from internal compiler transformations and public API publication. Explicit metadata updates may change the requested metadata while recording the change; they do not erase origin/hygiene/context or make stale facts current. Reject the following false substitutes: An internal compiler transform fixture does not prove the published syntax API actually calls it. Publishing an export or returning raw form data does not preserve syntax context. with-syntax-meta is an explicit update, not a promise that all metadata bytes are unchanged. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/meta/stable-ir-inspection: Expose authorized stable public IR inspection views while distinguishing or rejecting unstable compiler-internal mutation. Negative fixtures: Reject ungranted inspection, unstable internal views advertised stable and mutation through a read-only public inspection API. Required outputs: Versioned public IR views, allowed inspection and internal-mutation/authority refusals. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. |\n| Implement cryptographic adapters | [Module inventory](../phase-16-standard-library/README.md) | Own the STD18 public library boundary: Execute the declared cryptographic provider through the typed audited public wrapper. Required outputs: Callable cryptographic lifecycle/hybrid/protected-value API with provider/trust/redaction evidence. Negative acceptance: Reject invalid key/credential lifecycle, wrong hybrid binding, missing review and secret leakage. Consume actual interface artifacts from crypto, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; naming a service does not implement it or require whole-component completion. Shared adapter source conditions below apply only to this API's subject, not its siblings. Implementation acceptance remains Open. Decision criterion interface/domain/crypto-provider-binding: Bind cryptographic operations/parsers/randomness to declared algorithms, versions, parameters, secure randomness, capability, safe FFI and test-vector/audit contracts. Negative fixtures: Reject provider-chosen defaults, mismatched algorithm/mode/key/nonce/output policy, unavailable required secure entropy, ungranted FFI and unaudited experimental algorithms. Required outputs: Algorithm/provider/parameter/randomness manifest, known-answer vectors and authority/refusal records. Bind exact source/compiler