e/refusal matrix. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/crypto/hybrid-establishment-binding: Bind classical and post-quantum components, keys/ciphertexts, transcript/provider context, combiner/KDF and failure/downgrade handling before deriving application keys. Negative fixtures: Reject mismatched components/keys/ciphertexts/transcript/provider/combiner/KDF, partial-failure success, downgrade or deriving application keys before binding verification. Required outputs: Hybrid vectors, transcript/combiner records and mismatch/failure/downgrade fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/crypto/migration-inventory: Emit a complete algorithm-bearing surface inventory with replacement targets, deadlines, compatibility, verification and old-artifact disposition. Negative fixtures: Reject omitted algorithm-bearing surfaces, missing replacement/deadline/compatibility/verification policy or unresolved old-artifact disposition presented as migrated. Required outputs: Algorithm inventory and replacement/deadline/compatibility/verification/old-artifact migration report. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/platform/random-provider-kinds: Distinguish cryptographic entropy, deterministic PRNG, test seeds and host randomness, rejecting unavailable secure entropy where the actual operation requires it. Negative fixtures: Reject treating test seeds/PRNG/host randomness as secure entropy or proceeding when the operation requires unavailable secure entropy. Required outputs: Declared randomness-kind/provider records and secure-entropy availability/refusal fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. |\n| Implement UI and event adapters | [Module inventory](../phase-16-standard-library/README.md) | Own the STD19 public library boundary: Render and update through the library API and its declared runtime adapter with exact event/source identity. Required outputs: Callable typed UI/state/event/render API with accessibility, routing and trusted-sink behavior. Negative acceptance: Reject invalid events, unsafe render/DOM sinks, ungranted actions and missing required accessibility behavior. Consume actual interface artifacts from ui; naming a service does not implement it or require whole-component completion. Shared adapter source conditions below apply only to this API's subject, not its siblings. Implementation acceptance remains Open. Retain the standard rendering boundary that distinguishes escaped text, trusted markup, binary media and native views, and enforces the selected sink's trust policy. Actual web DOM/render-event execution is one qualified consumer; native/terminal/media adapters have their declared target rules. Reuse actual adapter checks without treating a web-only unsafe-DOM fixture or public rendering API inventory as universal rendering conformance. Reject the following false substitutes: A typed render export alone does not reject unsafe markup at an actual sink. HTML escaping is not a universal native-view, media or terminal trust rule. An event/schema fixture does not establish the rendering kind distinction or adapter invocation. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/ui/component-artifact-production: Produce typed component artifacts