   "Own the STD11 public library boundary: Execute the declared provider through the public typed database API. Required outputs: Callable prepared query/row/transaction API and commit/rollback/retry/isolation results. Negative acceptance: Reject unparameterized tainted queries, invalid rows, missing grants and broken transaction semantics. Consume actual interface artifacts from query, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; naming a service does not implement it or require whole-component completion. Shared adapter source conditions below apply only to this API's subject, not its siblings. Implementation acceptance remains Open. The broad query outcome lowers/executes a typed query and validates rows/failures under declared transaction/provider semantics. STD11 additionally requires the standard transaction API to execute commit, rollback, retry and isolation/idempotency behavior. Retain that concrete lifecycle outcome under the existing adapters task; a provider transaction implementation may be shared but its invocation and observable transitions through the standard API require their own acceptance. Reject the following false substitutes: A parameterized SELECT returning typed rows proves no commit/rollback path. Transaction metadata or a named commit export does not execute the transaction. Retry must follow declared isolation, idempotency and provider failure policy; it is not an invented retry allowance. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/db/parameterized-query-construction: Construct a typed query with untrusted values in explicit bound parameters separate from query structure, retaining the result row-schema reference. Negative fixtures: Reject untrusted interpolation into query structure, unbound values and missing/mismatched result-row schema identity. Required outputs: Typed query structure, separate parameter bindings and row-schema identity with injection/refusal fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred."}
