   "Own the STD15 public library boundary: Invoke the public meta API against actual syntax and compiler services under declared scoped authority. Required outputs: Callable compiler/syntax inspection/transform API preserving phases, hygiene, source, metadata and pass invalidation. Negative acceptance: Reject hidden compiler mutation, lost origins/hygiene, stale facts and ungranted phase access. Consume actual interface artifacts from syntax/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/syntax5-integrate-consumers, pipeline, plugins; naming a service does not implement it or require whole-component completion. Shared adapter source conditions below apply only to this API's subject, not its siblings. Implementation acceptance remains Open. STD15 requires actual syntax construction/inspection/transform APIs to preserve spans, hygiene, namespace, metadata and phase; C3 defines the underlying syntax representation and internal transform rules. Retain the library-call outcome separately from internal compiler transformations and public API publication. Explicit metadata updates may change the requested metadata while recording the change; they do not erase origin/hygiene/context or make stale facts current. Reject the following false substitutes: An internal compiler transform fixture does not prove the published syntax API actually calls it. Publishing an export or returning raw form data does not preserve syntax context. with-syntax-meta is an explicit update, not a promise that all metadata bytes are unchanged. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/meta/stable-ir-inspection: Expose authorized stable public IR inspection views while distinguishing or rejecting unstable compiler-internal mutation. Negative fixtures: Reject ungranted inspection, unstable internal views advertised stable and mutation through a read-only public inspection API. Required outputs: Versioned public IR views, allowed inspection and internal-mutation/authority refusals. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred."}
